    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5207123b_d42c6777",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1273,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-10T23:06:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is to provide a memory barrier to prevent a very unlikely but theoretically possible race: the VMM in thread 1 sets `pvmfw_load_addr` via the `KVM_CAP_X86_PROTECTED_VM_FLAGS_SET_FW_GPA` ioctl and then in thread 2 on another CPU makes the `PKVM_HC_FINALIZE_SHADOW_VM` hypercall, and `__pkvm_finalize_shadow_vm()` on that CPU sees the old value of `pvmfw_load_addr` instead of the new value set by thread 1.\n\nIn ARM code the memory barrier is provided by `mutex_unlock(\u0026kvm-\u003elock)`, while here in x86 code we don\u0027t lock `kvm-\u003elock` since we don\u0027t have a particular need to lock it.",
      "parentUuid": "d69ecc74_8ab6d75c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1273,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1273,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "cb3a5ed1e0408f209368f974969d2b3d34a3a21d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9114b714_027eb1fc",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
